docs {
  # Batch Get Access URLs

  **Method:** `POST`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/attachments/batch/urls`
  **Auth:** Required (Bearer Token)

  ## Description

  Fetches active access URLs for a list of attachment IDs concurrently. For private files, generates freshly signed presigned GET URLs with the specified expiration. For public files, returns direct public URLs.

  ## Request

  ### Query Parameters

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `expiry` | `string` | No | URL expiration duration (e.g. `15m`, `1h`, `24h`; defaults to `1h`) |

  ### Headers

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`) |
  | `Content-Type` | `string` | Yes | `application/json` |

  ### Body

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `attachment_ids` | `int64[]` | Yes | List of attachment IDs (max 100) |

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "urls": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "access_url": "https://storage.example.com/uploads/photo.jpg?X-Amz-Signature=...",
          "expires_at": "2026-11-02T20:00:00Z"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  * `400 Bad Request` — Empty attachment IDs list or exceeds limit (100)
  * `401 Unauthorized` — Missing or invalid token
  * `403 Forbidden` — Access denied to one or more private attachments
}
